normal mode beforehand.

00:31:57.720 --> 00:32:00.530
- Yeah. And I'm curious
your thoughts on this

00:32:00.530 --> 00:32:04.860
because it's something
I've been thinking about

00:32:04.860 --> 00:32:08.300
I don't know, by how like
a concrete take on it

00:32:08.300 --> 00:32:13.000
but it's great that anxiety, depression

00:32:13.850 --> 00:32:16.370
all these things are being normalized.

00:32:16.370 --> 00:32:18.960
However, sometimes I wonder

00:32:18.960 --> 00:32:23.950
if someone experiences nervousness
and says I have anxiety

00:32:23.950 --> 00:32:27.530
or experiences sadness
and says I'm depressed.

00:32:27.530 --> 00:32:30.430
And it's tough because if
someone says they're anxious

00:32:30.430 --> 00:32:32.470
or depressed, you don't
wanna question that,

00:32:32.470 --> 00:32:35.000
you wanna validate that
and take their word for it.

00:32:35.000 --> 00:32:36.640
That's so important.

00:32:36.640 --> 00:32:39.810
However, are we getting to sensitize

00:32:39.810 --> 00:32:43.110
to what like the actual
mental illness are and the

00:32:43.110 --> 00:32:46.520
what the concrete diagnosable
mental health issues are?

00:32:46.520 --> 00:32:50.570
And as a result are some of
the people who are just nervous

00:32:50.570 --> 00:32:55.440
or just sad kind of maybe
giving up too soon on the fact

00:32:55.440 --> 00:32:58.658
that they could do some work there

00:32:58.658 --> 00:33:01.140
to get back to a place they wanna be.

00:33:01.140 --> 00:33:04.880
I almost think people are so focused

00:33:04.880 --> 00:33:08.390
on being happy all the time at
the minute and emotion comes

00:33:08.390 --> 00:33:09.700
that's not happiness.

00:33:09.700 --> 00:33:13.560
We wanna label it as something
that maybe it's not yet.

00:33:13.560 --> 00:33:18.410
And I know that that's
like controversial to say.

00:33:18.410 --> 00:33:20.890
I just think it's an important component.

00:33:20.890 --> 00:33:22.417
- Yeah, I think it's a
really good question.

00:33:22.417 --> 00:33:24.660
I'll be a little bit speculative

00:33:24.660 --> 00:33:25.550
in that sense as well

00:33:25.550 --> 00:33:28.390
but I think you're onto something as well.

00:33:28.390 --> 00:33:30.290
So I mean, from a clinical standpoint

00:33:30.290 --> 00:33:32.340
whenever people are in
the clinical situation

00:33:32.340 --> 00:33:33.660
with clinical anxiety, you know

00:33:33.660 --> 00:33:36.140
generalized anxiety disorder
or depression kind of one

00:33:36.140 --> 00:33:41.140
of the hallmarks within therapy
is not to avoid the anxiety

00:33:41.180 --> 00:33:42.710
because that just lets it sit.

00:33:42.710 --> 00:33:44.860
So there's lots of ways that psychologists

00:33:44.860 --> 00:33:46.640
kind of walk people
through that to kind of

00:33:46.640 --> 00:33:48.880
you can do exposure theory to kind of walk

00:33:48.880 --> 00:33:51.270
up to things over time
and kind of deal with it.

00:33:51.270 --> 00:33:53.370
But the reason I bring that
up it's I think it ties in

00:33:53.370 --> 00:33:55.980
to what you're mentioning as
well when people are talking

00:33:55.980 --> 00:33:59.150
about times of being
anxious or feeling sad.

00:33:59.150 --> 00:34:00.783
And so there's a line there
and this is a specular part.

00:34:00.783 --> 00:34:03.970
There's a line to walk where
you don't want people who are

00:34:03.970 --> 00:34:08.430
feeling that to just avoid it
because that in itself is not

00:34:08.430 --> 00:34:10.320
necessarily healthy because
in some ways, you know

00:34:10.320 --> 00:34:12.700
some aspects of anxiety are good for us.

00:34:12.700 --> 00:34:14.220
It kind of helps us geer up.

00:34:14.220 --> 00:34:17.020
So you know from a classroom
setting and people often talk

00:34:17.020 --> 00:34:18.290
about if you're getting
a little bit anxious

00:34:18.290 --> 00:34:19.380
about a test that's probably good.

00:34:19.380 --> 00:34:20.680
It would probably encourage you to study

00:34:20.680 --> 00:34:22.210
and not just wing it.

00:34:22.210 --> 00:34:23.270
So there's a ramping up.

00:34:23.270 --> 00:34:25.220
It kind of forcing you
to take that seriously.

00:34:25.220 --> 00:34:28.820
Or if someone's giving a talk
in front of 100,000 people,

00:34:28.820 --> 00:34:30.160
there's probably gonna be some anxiety

00:34:30.160 --> 00:34:32.090
but that's not necessarily bad.

00:34:32.090 --> 00:34:34.980
It can kind of help them
elevate their performance.

00:34:34.980 --> 00:34:35.890
So you know that can come in

00:34:35.890 --> 00:34:37.070
with sports environments as well.

00:34:37.070 --> 00:34:39.440
But I do think there is a line to walk.

00:34:39.440 --> 00:34:42.330
And I don't know if I have a
clear answer for you in terms

00:34:42.330 --> 00:34:46.550
of making sure that people
are empowered to still move

00:34:46.550 --> 00:34:47.840
through those things.

00:34:47.840 --> 00:34:49.472
So like you said you have to validate it.

00:34:49.472 --> 00:34:50.883
You don't want to be dismissive of it

00:34:50.883 --> 00:34:52.747
because you don't know the
level of depth that it is,

00:34:52.747 --> 00:34:53.940
but at the same time

00:34:53.940 --> 00:34:55.910
you don't want people to
be and maybe this is where

00:34:55.910 --> 00:34:58.650
you're going with your question
to be hampered by that.

00:34:58.650 --> 00:34:59.483
- Yeah.

00:34:59.483 --> 00:35:02.120
Sometimes I think mental
health issues or mental illness

00:35:02.120 --> 00:35:04.568
or eating disorders can become glamorized.

00:35:04.568 --> 00:35:09.568
And you see people wanting
to have that issue.

00:35:10.460 --> 00:35:13.760
And I don't know, like
I said I don't have a

00:35:13.760 --> 00:35:15.330
it's something I've noticed

00:35:15.330 --> 00:35:17.563
and I don't have like a take on it.

00:35:19.160 --> 00:35:21.180
I just think it's worth thinking

00:35:21.180 --> 00:35:26.180
about because it's important
to the conversation.

00:35:27.310 --> 00:35:28.143
- I agree.

00:35:28.143 --> 00:35:29.080
And I think that comes down

00:35:29.080 --> 00:35:30.710
